 {
  "n": 89,
  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 119.0,
  "event_seq": 280,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute ticket volume doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1220/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-02), not because response handling is slow (E-01: median 1.6d/p90 2.8d within 3.0d SLA) or a tariff change (E-06), but because billing-import rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 (E-13), compares raw AMI register values directly against 12-month m3-based consumption history with no unit scaling; firmware v4.2 meters (rolled out June 2026) report register values in 0.1 m3 units versus v3.x's plain m3 (E-14), so BV-17 misclassifies valid on-time v4.2 reads as high-consumption and rejects them at import (E-12: 1184/1240 ESTIMATED-type disputed bills had an on-time read rejected this way), forcing estimate substitution and wrong bills for those accounts. This explains the ESTIMATED-type share of disputes (1240/3025, E-04) but not the larger ACTUAL-type share (1785/3025, E-04), whose cause remains unestablished."
 },
